# the oracle lane of the link-edit codecs, one blob per run
#
# `linkedit <kind> <blob> <pointer width> [segment prefix]` decodes the
# link-edit blob in the file and encodes the entries back, and exits 0 when
# the bytes come out as they went in. `linkedit read <file>` reads a whole
# Mach-O file, fat or thin, and prints a line for each link-edit blob, unwind
# section and signature blob: `entries <what>` when the reader holds it as
# entries, or `raw <what> <why>` when it holds the bytes. kinds are rebase, bind, lazy, weak,
# export, starts, dic, chained, sig, unwind_info and compact_unwind. for
# chained, every segment file `<segment prefix><n>` is also walked and each
# pointer packed again. tools/macho/linkedit.sh cuts the blobs out of Mach-O
# files and drives this. it runs locally and is never part of CI.

